1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,025
This Archify map explains the released Focus
Tube architecture and the choices behind it.

2
00:00:05,025 --> 00:00:09,794
It is linked to the documented release
source, not to a live production inspection.

3
00:00:09,794 --> 00:00:16,319
The highlighted path runs from the browser, through
Express security checks and feature handlers, into SQLite.

4
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:22,972
The boxes inside the instance boundary are logical
responsibilities, not separately deployed microservices.

5
00:00:22,972 --> 00:00:25,802
Animated paths illustrate those relationships.

6
00:00:25,802 --> 00:00:28,378
They are not measured requests or live traffic.

7
00:00:28,378 --> 00:00:34,475
We will separate the design rationale, its tradeoffs,
and later work that is not included in this baseline.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:43,578
The application uses a modular monolith: one Node and
Express process, with separate modules for identity, notes,

9
00:00:43,578 --> 00:00:46,042
chat, feedback, capture, and observability.

10
00:00:46,042 --> 00:00:49,024
This keeps self-hosting and local development small.

11
00:00:49,024 --> 00:00:54,491
There is no required message broker, Redis
service, or separate authentication deployment.

12
00:00:54,491 --> 00:01:00,456
Keeping related state in one process and database
also makes transactional operations straightforward.

13
00:01:00,456 --> 00:01:04,462
The tradeoff is shared process
capacity and coordinated releases.

14
00:01:04,462 --> 00:01:11,462
More infrastructure would only be justified by measured
workload or ownership needs, not by the diagram having several

15
00:01:11,462 --> 00:01:11,850
boxes.

16
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:16,967
The frontend is vanilla JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.

17
00:01:16,967 --> 00:01:24,231
Express serves the application, fonts, Lucide
icons, Quill, charts, and PDF tools locally.

18
00:01:24,231 --> 00:01:29,559
That avoids a separate frontend build server
and reduces routine third-party asset requests.

19
00:01:29,559 --> 00:01:37,000
The browser owns temporary interaction state, such as the
current route, panel visibility, selection, and unsent

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,465
drafts.

21
00:01:37,465 --> 00:01:40,403
The server owns durable account and learning records.

22
00:01:40,403 --> 00:01:46,539
This small stack still needs discipline: imperative code
must cancel stale work, preserve editor instances, and

23
00:01:46,539 --> 00:01:50,757
prevent a response from one account
or course painting over another.

24
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:56,204
Authentication uses salted scrypt
password hashes and opaque session tokens.

25
00:01:56,204 --> 00:02:04,337
Only token hashes are stored, and the browser receives an
HttpOnly cookie with strict same-site behavior and Secure on

26
00:02:04,337 --> 00:02:04,765
HTTPS.

27
00:02:04,765 --> 00:02:10,116
This allows explicit server-side revocation
instead of trusting a browser token indefinitely.

28
00:02:10,116 --> 00:02:13,793
Exact Host and Origin checks sit alongside authentication.

29
00:02:13,793 --> 00:02:18,271
Account-binding headers help reject
stale tabs, but are not credentials.

30
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:25,663
Invitations, email proof, username uniqueness, capacity,
account creation, and session issuance are rechecked

31
00:02:25,663 --> 00:02:26,232
together.

32
00:02:26,232 --> 00:02:31,210
A failed registration must not spend an
invitation or consume a valid proof partially.

33
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:36,479
SQLite provides a durable local database
without another server to provision.

34
00:02:36,479 --> 00:02:43,790
Write-ahead logging, foreign keys, bounded busy waits,
and immediate transactions give the application a concrete

35
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:44,764
consistency boundary.

36
00:02:44,764 --> 00:02:51,101
Profiles hold revisioned course and planning data, while
notes and conversations have their own records and revisions.

37
00:02:51,101 --> 00:02:57,994
An invitation redemption, capture receipt, or AI
reservation can succeed atomically with its related changes.

38
00:02:57,994 --> 00:03:01,627
The important tradeoff is that SQLite serializes writes.

39
00:03:01,627 --> 00:03:08,171
A larger deployment would need measured capacity
planning, and potentially a different database or workload

40
00:03:08,171 --> 00:03:11,225
architecture, rather than assuming
unlimited horizontal scaling.

41
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:18,133
Notes use a validated document model around Quill
instead of treating arbitrary HTML as trusted storage.

42
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:24,934
Source anchors attach to paragraphs only when the matching
player supplies a real timestamp; zero seconds remains

43
00:03:24,934 --> 00:03:25,334
valid.

44
00:03:25,334 --> 00:03:29,673
A local edit updates recovery state,
then sends a revision-checked save.

45
00:03:29,673 --> 00:03:32,346
Saved means the server acknowledged that revision.

46
00:03:32,346 --> 00:03:37,958
New edits during a request remain dirty, and
conflicting revisions require an explicit choice.

47
00:03:37,958 --> 00:03:44,728
Separating document state from pane visibility lets the
user resize, switch views, or move between Chat and Notes

48
00:03:44,728 --> 00:03:47,736
without recreating the editor or losing its history.

49
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:55,068
YouTube's official embedded player owns playback,
including its speed, quality, and content restrictions.

50
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:58,957
Public metadata and permitted
captions are separate retrieval paths.

51
00:03:58,957 --> 00:04:04,505
Chat sends bounded caption context and the selected
conversation to Google only after permission.

52
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:08,635
It does not automatically send
existing notebooks or unrelated videos.

53
00:04:08,635 --> 00:04:14,995
The browser can show provisional streamed text, but only
a validated final answer is persisted and can expose

54
00:04:14,995 --> 00:04:16,762
citations or a note preview.

55
00:04:16,762 --> 00:04:20,499
This boundary avoids presenting
partial output as durable work.

56
00:04:20,499 --> 00:04:27,177
It also makes the limitations explicit: missing captions
and provider failures are real failures, not reasons to

57
00:04:27,177 --> 00:04:28,356
invent a source.

58
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:35,127
The released quota policy allows thirty admitted requests
per account in a six-hour window, alongside the short-term

59
00:04:35,127 --> 00:04:37,992
rate limit and one active answer per account.

60
00:04:37,992 --> 00:04:42,284
SQLite reserves a request slot and
estimated maximum cost together.

61
00:04:42,284 --> 00:04:47,428
The first admitted request starts the window;
later requests do not move its deadline.

62
00:04:47,428 --> 00:04:50,029
The shared monthly cost ledger is independent.

63
00:04:50,029 --> 00:04:54,275
A full personal allowance can still be
blocked by insufficient budget headroom.

64
00:04:54,275 --> 00:05:00,676
Known usage is reconciled, while unknown usage after
a failed or canceled call can retain the reservation.

65
00:05:00,676 --> 00:05:05,363
Replaying the same completed request does
not generate twice or spend another slot.

66
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:13,017
The Manifest version three extension has a narrow job: add
one chosen video to one selected Focus Tube environment.

67
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:19,327
Optional host permissions, exact extension identity,
and account-bound operations limit its reach.

68
00:05:19,327 --> 00:05:21,611
It tries the existing session first.

69
00:05:21,611 --> 00:05:28,608
Where browser policy requires a separate connection, the
first-party consent flow uses state, PKCE, a single-use code,

70
00:05:28,608 --> 00:05:32,724
and a scoped opaque grant bounded by its parent session.

71
00:05:32,724 --> 00:05:38,137
Saves are additive and return idempotent
receipts, rather than replacing the whole profile.

72
00:05:38,137 --> 00:05:44,531
A bounded queue supports manual recovery without silently
retrying forever or changing the destination account.

73
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:52,322
Feedback is a separate public and private forum, with
authorization checked again for reports, replies, and

74
00:05:52,322 --> 00:05:52,765
screenshots.

75
00:05:52,765 --> 00:05:58,138
Sharp validates and normalizes selected images,
and storage commits with the parent record.

76
00:05:58,138 --> 00:06:00,623
Public posting needs explicit consent.

77
00:06:00,623 --> 00:06:06,897
Operational logs and metrics are bounded and sanitized;
private scrape credentials are separate from an

78
00:06:06,897 --> 00:06:07,734
administrator's session.

79
00:06:07,734 --> 00:06:12,175
Optional audience and usage analytics have
their own consent and retention rules.

80
00:06:12,175 --> 00:06:16,492
These choices distinguish troubleshooting
from collecting private learning content.

81
00:06:16,492 --> 00:06:23,446
They also preserve an important limit: removing image metadata
does not remove a password that is visibly present in a

82
00:06:23,446 --> 00:06:23,794
screenshot.

83
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:31,822
Docker Compose keeps local, development, and production
configurations explicit, with separate projects and persistent

84
00:06:31,822 --> 00:06:32,876
data volumes.

85
00:06:32,876 --> 00:06:40,955
A learning export is not a full operational backup: it
excludes credentials, sessions, grants, shared feedback, and

86
00:06:40,955 --> 00:06:41,905
spending records.

87
00:06:41,905 --> 00:06:47,858
Instance recovery needs a consistent SQLite
backup and securely managed runtime configuration.

88
00:06:47,858 --> 00:06:54,971
The documented branch-triggered deployment jobs build and
start services, but do not automatically prove every test,

89
00:06:54,971 --> 00:06:57,193
backup, health, or acceptance gate.

90
00:06:57,193 --> 00:07:00,220
A green job is therefore not the whole release decision.

91
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:06,875
Safe rollout still means a scoped artifact, verified
data preservation, and an explicit rollback plan.

92
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:14,418
Newer uncommitted work explores an answer cache with exact
private-context matching and tightly constrained sharing of

93
00:07:14,418 --> 00:07:15,712
canonical public-source answers.

94
00:07:15,712 --> 00:07:22,589
Semantic matching remains gated on real calibration,
so it should not be described as a validated production

95
00:07:22,589 --> 00:07:22,994
capability.

96
00:07:22,994 --> 00:07:29,313
Social sign-in and the motion integration plan are also
separate proposals, not facts inferred from this map.

97
00:07:29,313 --> 00:07:34,317
The recurring design principle is to keep
state ownership and failure behavior explicit.

98
00:07:34,317 --> 00:07:41,215
Start small, preserve user control, and add complexity only
when there is a measured reason and a testable contract.
